<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.mirai-station.spx-jev-premarket</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>-lc</string>
    <string>$HOME/.claude/plugins/mirai-station/runtime/scripts/run-spx-jev-premarket.sh</string>
  </array>

  <!-- The SPX premarket lane: a read at each checkpoint before the open, 02:35, 03:35, 08:05, 08:48,
       09:05 and 09:28 ET, each saving the overnight futures and building the night's labels, JEV asked
       only at the reads its questions name; then once at 10:06 ET, the close-out, which asks JEV nothing
       and grades the morning's calls from the settled open (spx_jev/lane.py PREMARKET.schedule and
       close_out, spx_jev/premarket.py checkpoints; a test holds these entries to them). It also fires at
       04:35 ET, Europe's checkpoint in a week Frankfurt keeps winter time and New York does not; the
       command reads only the day's own checkpoints and refuses a fire more than 5 minutes late, so the
       04:35 fire reads nothing in any other week, and the 03:35 one nothing in that week. Writes only
       state/spx_jev/lanes/premarket/, its lines in the archive, and the overnight store.
       NOTE: launchd's StartCalendarInterval uses SYSTEM-LOCAL time and ignores the
       TZ env var below. This box runs on Pacific, so Hour=5 Minute=48 == 05:48 PT == 08:48 ET
       year-round (PT is ET minus 3h through DST). 02:35 ET is 23:35 PT the evening before, so its
       entries run Sunday (Weekday 0) to Thursday; every other fire runs Monday to Friday. -->
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <array>
    <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>0</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>23</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>35</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>1</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>23</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>35</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>2</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>23</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>35</integer></dict>
